  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The gauntlet – get past the gladiators",
  "description": "Split the rink into three zones skating from board to board, with one gladiator in each zone. The gladiators may only move within their own zone. Everyone else starts at one end with a puck each. On the signal they skate with the puck through all the zones to the other end without a gladiator taking it.\n\nLose the puck and you fetch a new one and try again. Progression: whoever loses the puck becomes a gladiator in the zone where it happened. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Find the space where the gladiator is not."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "High speed on the straight, short touches near the gladiator."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "How do you hold the stick when you want to skate as fast as you can?"
    }
  ],
